{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\WINDOWS\\\\System32\\\\WindowsPowerShell\\\\v1.0\\\\powershell.exe\" -Command '$i=0; Get-Content -LiteralPath '\"'RESULTS.md' | ForEach-Object { \"'$i++; '\"'{0,4}: {1}' -f \"'$i, $_ }'","aggregated_output":"   1: # Recipe Execution Results\r\n   2: \r\n   3: This file records measured VRAM and runtime performance for every recipe variant.\r\n   4: **Hard Gate Ceiling**: **14.5 GB** (14,848 MiB) physical VRAM peak limit on NVIDIA GeForce RTX 5080 Laptop GPU.\r\n   5: \r\n   6: | recipe | status | peak VRAM (GB) | baseline VRAM (GB) | wall clock (s) | notes |\r\n   7: |---|---|---|---|---|---|\r\n   8: | `t2i_low` | **PASS** | 11.64 | 1.88 | 7.7 | Warm cache (Run #10); boot lane: lab-8199, sage-free |\r\n   9: | `t2i_high` | **PASS** | 13.12 | 1.89 | 6.7 | Warm cache (Run #4); boot lane: lab-8199, sage-free |\r\n  10: | `wan_ti2v_low` | **PASS** | 13.15 | 1.80 | 14.6 | Wan 2.2 5B Q5_K_M GGUF (`UnetLoaderGGUF`); warm cache (Run #2) |\r\n  11: | `wan_ti2v_high` | **FAIL** | 15.55 | 2.06 | 46.3 | Wan 2.2 5B Q5_K_M GGUF; peak VRAM 15.55 GB > 14.5 GB gate line |\r\n  12: | `wan_i2v_14b_low` | **FAIL** | 15.28 | 1.66 | 19.7 | Wan 2.2 14B FP8; peak VRAM 15.28 GB > 14.5 GB gate line |\r\n  13: | `wan_i2v_14b_high` | **FAIL** | 15.34 | 1.19 | 30.0 | Wan 2.2 14B FP8; peak VRAM 15.34 GB > 14.5 GB gate line |\r\n  14: | `ltx_i2v_low` | **ERROR** | 10.84 | 1.75 | 7.5 | Wiring/graph fault: LTXAV embedding shape mismatch |\r\n  15: | `ltx_i2v_high` | **ERROR** | 10.51 | 1.31 | 6.1 | Wiring/graph fault: LTXAV embedding shape mismatch |\r\n  16: | `ltx_audio_low` | **ERROR** | 10.82 | 1.51 | 4.5 | Wiring/graph fault: LTXAV audio connector shape mismatch |\r\n  17: | `ltx_lipsync_low` | **BLOCKED** | 0.00 | 0.00 | 0.0 | Missing HuMo/lip-sync custom nodes on server |\r\n  18: | `h3_t2v_low` | **BLOCKED** | 0.00 | 0.00 | 0.0 | 864x480 x 124f; weights missing (42.5 GB); EXTERNAL-REPORTED peak 7.4-7.6 GB |\r\n  19: | `h3_t2v_best` | **BLOCKED** | 0.00 | 0.00 | 0.0 | 864x480 x 124f; weights missing (42.5 GB); EXTERNAL-REPORTED peak 7.4-7.6 GB |\r\n  20: | `h3_i2v_low` | **BLOCKED** | 0.00 | 0.00 | 0.0 | 864x480 x 124f; weights missing (42.5 GB); EXTERNAL-REPORTED peak 7.4-7.6 GB |\r\n  21: | `h3_i2v_best` | **BLOCKED** | 0.00 | 0.00 | 0.0 | 864x480 x 124f; weights missing (42.5 GB); EXTERNAL-REPORTED peak 7.4-7.6 GB |\r\n  22: | `h3_r2v_low` | **BLOCKED** | 0.00 | 0.00 | 0.0 | 864x480 x 124f; weights missing (42.5 GB); EXTERNAL-REPORTED peak 7.4-7.6 GB |\r\n  23: | `h3_r2v_best` | **BLOCKED** | 0.00 | 0.00 | 0.0 | 864x480 x 124f; weights missing (42.5 GB); EXTERNAL-REPORTED peak 7.4-7.6 GB |\r\n  24: | t2i_low | PASS | 12.32 | 1.90 | 7.3 | Run #11; boot lane: lab-8199, sage-free |\r\n  25: | t2i_high | PASS | 13.15 | 1.90 | 6.3 | Run #5; boot lane: lab-8199, sage-free |\r\n  26: | wan_ti2v_low | PASS | 12.46 | 1.47 | 13.8 | Run #7; boot lane: lab-8199, sage-free |\r\n  27: | wan_ti2v_high | FAIL | 0.00 | 0.00 | 0.0 | Aborted on Preflight #7 (Affordability estimate): Last measured peak (15.55 GB) exceeded 14.5 GB gate line. Refusing unchanged re-run. |\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\WINDOWS\\\\System32\\\\WindowsPowerShell\\\\v1.0\\\\powershell.exe\" -Command '$i=0; Get-Content -LiteralPath '\"'PREFLIGHT.md' | ForEach-Object { \"'$i++; '\"'{0,4}: {1}' -f \"'$i, $_ }'","aggregated_output":"   1: # Preflight Checklist\r\n   2: \r\n   3: Run BEFORE queuing every clip ƒ?\" implemented in code inside `run_recipe.py`, not performed by hand. Any failed check aborts the run with a named reason; nothing gets queued on a failed preflight.\r\n   4: \r\n   5: Context: OTR shipped three engines whose VRAM preflight guard (`assert_frame_affordable`) was written but never called ƒ?\" every coverage-planned segment renders unchecked, and an in-process CUDA OOM corrupts the allocator (see `research/2026-08-03-PROBLEM-STATEMENT-minimax-h3.md`, section 4, F1). This lab does not repeat that mistake. The preflight is wired in from day one and `run_recipe.py` refuses to queue without it.\r\n   6: \r\n   7: 1. **Lock** ƒ?\" `.gpu.lock` does not exist. Create it atomically (`O_CREAT | O_EXCL`); store PID and timestamp; remove on exit, even on error.\r\n   8: 2. **GPU idle & Host RAM tracking** ƒ?\" `nvidia-smi` shows under **2.5 GB (2560 MB)** allocated VRAM. System Host RAM (`psutil.virtual_memory()`) is recorded as baseline host RAM and tracked concurrently at 200ms intervals throughout execution. If another process is using the GPU (> 2.5 GB allocated), abort; do not queue behind it.\r\n   9: 3. **Server up / Lab Server Ownership** ƒ?\" `GET /system_stats` answers at `127.0.0.1:8199`.\r\n  10:    - If port 8199 answers BUT no PID receipt (`.server.pid`) exists from this session, abort with reason: `Unrecognized server answering on 8199 without PID receipt` (do NOT adopt or kill it).\r\n  11:    - If port 8199 is down, launch `boot_lab_server.cmd` detached, write `.server.pid`, and health-check `GET http://127.0.0.1:8199/system_stats` every 3s up to 120s. On boot failure, read tail of `server.log` and report real error.\r\n  12: 4. **Nodes exist** ƒ?\" every `class_type` in the recipe appears in `GET /object_info` at `127.0.0.1:8199`. Missing node = BLOCKED, never an install.\r\n  13: 5. **Models exist** ƒ?\" every model file the recipe references appears in `models_manifest.md`. Missing model = BLOCKED, never a download.\r\n  14: 6. **Widget integrity** ƒ?\" recipe JSON parses; every node's widget count matches its `widgets_values` length.\r\n  15: 7. **Affordability estimate** ƒ?\" before the first-ever run of a recipe, estimate VRAM from weights size + resolution x frame count and record it in the results entry. After a measured run exists, the measured peak replaces the estimate and the preflight refuses configurations whose last measured peak exceeded 14.5 GB (no re-running known-failing configs unchanged).\r\n  16: 8. **Fixtures uploaded** ƒ?\" required fixtures are present on disk and uploaded to server input directory via `POST /upload/image`. Never regenerate a fixture.\r\n  17: 9. **Boot lane** ƒ?\" confirm boot lane is `lab-8199, sage-free` (server started without `--use-sage-attention`). Record the boot lane in the results entry.\r\n  18: 10. **Disk** ƒ?\" at least 5 GB free on the output drive.\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\WINDOWS\\\\System32\\\\WindowsPowerShell\\\\v1.0\\\\powershell.exe\" -Command '$i=0; Get-Content -LiteralPath '\"'docs\\\\ltx_wan_failures_review.md' | ForEach-Object { \"'$i++; '\"'{0,4}: {1}' -f \"'$i, $_ }'","aggregated_output":"   1: # Recipe Failure Diagnostics ƒ?\" LTX-Video & Wan-Video Suite\r\n   2: \r\n   3: ## Context & Invariants\r\n   4: - Platform: Windows 11, RTX 5080 Laptop (16 GB physical VRAM, 14.5 GB strict lab ceiling)\r\n   5: - Torch 2.10.0 + CUDA 13.0 + SageAttention + SDPA\r\n   6: - Hardware VRAM Ceiling: 14.5 GB max peak across all runs\r\n   7: - Boot Lane: headless ComfyUI on port 8199 (`boot_lab_server.cmd`)\r\n   8: \r\n   9: ## Issue 1: `ltx_i2v_low` & `ltx_i2v_high` Execution Error\r\n  10: Executing `ltx_i2v_low` triggers a RuntimeError inside KSampler (Node 8):\r\n  11: ```\r\n  12: RuntimeError: Sizes of tensors must match except in dimension 1. Expected size 4096 but got size 2048 for tensor number 1 in the list.\r\n  13: Traceback:\r\n  14:   File \"comfy/ldm/lightricks/av_model.py\", line 579, in preprocess_text_embeds\r\n  15:     out_audio = self.audio_embeddings_connector(context_audio)[0]\r\n  16:   File \"comfy/ldm/lightricks/embeddings_connector.py\", line 286, in forward\r\n  17:     hidden_states = torch.cat((hidden_states, learnable_registers[hidden_states.shape[1]:].unsqueeze(0).repeat(hidden_states.shape[0], 1, 1)), dim=1)\r\n  18: ```\r\n  19: Questions:\r\n  20: 1. Is LTX-Video requiring a specific text encoder / clip model or audio embedding dimension?\r\n  21: 2. Are the dimensions of conditioning tensors from `CLIPTextEncode` or `LTXVConditioning` mismatched with what `ltx-video-2.0` expected?\r\n  22: \r\n  23: ## Issue 2: `wan_ti2v_high` & `wan_i2v_14b_low/high` Preflight #7 Block (VRAM Ceiling)\r\n  24: `run_recipe.py` Preflight Check #7 (Affordability Check) refuses to run recipes whose recorded `peak_vram_gb` in `results/<recipe>.json` exceeded 14.5 GB:\r\n  25: - `wan_ti2v_high`: last measured peak = 15.55 GB\r\n  26: - `wan_i2v_14b_low`: last measured peak = 15.28 GB\r\n  27: - `wan_i2v_14b_high`: last measured peak = 15.34 GB\r\n  28: \r\n  29: Questions:\r\n  30: 1. Can the 14B Wan recipes or 5B Q5 recipe be optimized (e.g. lowering resolution, frame count, or block swapping) to bring peak VRAM strictly <= 14.5 GB?\r\n  31: 2. How should `results/*.json` or recipe parameters be updated so preflight can re-test modified configurations?\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\WINDOWS\\\\System32\\\\WindowsPowerShell\\\\v1.0\\\\powershell.exe\" -Command '$i=0; Get-Content -LiteralPath '\"'run_recipe.py' | ForEach-Object { \"'$i++; '\"'{0,4}: {1}' -f \"'$i, $_ }'","aggregated_output":"   1: #!/usr/bin/env python3\r\n   2: \"\"\"\r\n   3: run_recipe.py ƒ?\" Recipe execution runner and preflight enforcement harness\r\n   4: for ComfyUI workflow VRAM recipe benchmarking.\r\n   5: \r\n   6: Talks to lab server at http://127.0.0.1:8199.\r\n   7: Self-boots lab server via boot_lab_server.cmd if down, tracking PID in .server.pid.\r\n   8: Windows 11 / RTX 5080 Laptop (16 GB, 14.5 GB gate ceiling).\r\n   9: \"\"\"\r\n  10: \r\n  11: import os\r\n  12: import sys\r\n  13: import time\r\n  14: import json\r\n  15: import psutil\r\n  16: import shutil\r\n  17: import urllib.request\r\n  18: import urllib.error\r\n  19: import subprocess\r\n  20: import threading\r\n  21: from pathlib import Path\r\n  22: from typing import Dict, Any, List, Tuple, Optional\r\n  23: \r\n  24: # --- Constants & Paths ---\r\n  25: REPO_ROOT = Path(__file__).parent.resolve()\r\n  26: LOCKFILE_PATH = REPO_ROOT / \".gpu.lock\"\r\n  27: SERVER_PID_FILE = REPO_ROOT / \".server.pid\"\r\n  28: SERVER_LOG_FILE = REPO_ROOT / \"server.log\"\r\n  29: BOOT_CMD = REPO_ROOT / \"boot_lab_server.cmd\"\r\n  30: RESULTS_DIR = REPO_ROOT / \"results\"\r\n  31: FIXTURES_DIR = REPO_ROOT / \"fixtures\"\r\n  32: MODELS_MANIFEST = REPO_ROOT / \"models_manifest.md\"\r\n  33: RESULTS_LEDGER = REPO_ROOT / \"RESULTS.md\"\r\n  34: ENGINE_MATRIX_BETA = REPO_ROOT / \"ENGINE_MATRIX_BETA.md\"\r\n  35: \r\n  36: LAB_PORT = os.environ.get(\"LAB_PORT\", \"8199\")\r\n  37: COMFY_SERVER_URL = f\"http://127.0.0.1:{LAB_PORT}\"\r\n  38: VRAM_GATE_GB = 14.5\r\n  39: VRAM_GPU_IDLE_MAX_MB = 2560  # 2.5 GB threshold\r\n  40: MIN_FREE_DISK_GB = 5.0\r\n  41: BOOT_TIMEOUT_S = 120\r\n  42: POLL_INTERVAL_S = 0.2  # 200ms VRAM polling interval\r\n  43: \r\n  44: \r\n  45: class PreflightError(Exception):\r\n  46:     \"\"\"Raised when a preflight check fails.\"\"\"\r\n  47:     def __init__(self, check_num: int, name: str, reason: str):\r\n  48:         self.check_num = check_num\r\n  49:         self.name = name\r\n  50:         self.reason = reason\r\n  51:         super().__init__(f\"Preflight Check #{check_num} [{name}] FAILED: {reason}\")\r\n  52: \r\n  53: \r\n  54: class LockManager:\r\n  55:     \"\"\"Atomic GPU Lockfile Manager with stale lock recovery.\"\"\"\r\n  56: \r\n  57:     def __init__(self, lock_path: Path = LOCKFILE_PATH):\r\n  58:         self.lock_path = lock_path\r\n  59:         self.acquired = False\r\n  60: \r\n  61:     def acquire(self):\r\n  62:         if self.lock_path.exists():\r\n  63:             try:\r\n  64:                 content = self.lock_path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8-sig\", errors=\"ignore\")\r\n  65:                 lock_info = json.loads(content)\r\n  66:                 pid = lock_info.get(\"pid\")\r\n  67:                 if pid and not psutil.pid_exists(pid):\r\n  68:                     print(f\"[LOCK] Removing stale lockfile from dead PID {pid}\")\r\n  69:                     self.lock_path.unlink(missing_ok=True)\r\n  70:                 else:\r\n  71:                     raise PreflightError(1, \"Lock\", f\".gpu.lock exists (held by PID {pid})\")\r\n  72:             except (json.JSONDecodeError, OSError):\r\n  73:                 raise PreflightError(1, \"Lock\", \".gpu.lock exists and cannot be read\")\r\n  74: \r\n  75:         try:\r\n  76:             fd = os.open(str(self.lock_path), os.O_CREAT | os.O_EXCL | os.O_WRONLY)\r\n  77:             lock_data = json.dumps({\"pid\": os.getpid(), \"time\": time.time()}).encode(\"utf-8\")\r\n  78:             os.write(fd, lock_data)\r\n  79:             os.close(fd)\r\n  80:             self.acquired = True\r\n  81:             print(f\"[LOCK] Acquired .gpu.lock (PID {os.getpid()})\")\r\n  82:         except OSError as e:\r\n  83:             raise PreflightError(1, \"Lock\", f\"Failed atomic lock acquisition: {e}\")\r\n  84: \r\n  85:     def release(self):\r\n  86:         if self.acquired and self.lock_path.exists():\r\n  87:             try:\r\n  88:                 self.lock_path.unlink()\r\n  89:                 print(\"[LOCK] Released .gpu.lock\")\r\n  90:             except OSError as e:\r\n  91:                 print(f\"[LOCK] Warning: failed to remove lockfile: {e}\")\r\n  92:             self.acquired = False\r\n  93: \r\n  94:     def __enter__(self):\r\n  95:         self.acquire()\r\n  96:         return self\r\n  97: \r\n  98:     def __exit__(self, exc_type, exc_val, exc_tb):\r\n  99:         self.release()\r\n 100: \r\n 101: \r\n 102: def query_gpu_vram_mb() -> float:\r\n 103:     \"\"\"Query current GPU VRAM usage in MB via nvidia-smi.\"\"\"\r\n 104:     res = subprocess.run(\r\n 105:         [\"nvidia-smi\", \"--query-gpu=memory.used\", \"--format=csv,noheader,nounits\"],\r\n 106:         capture_output=True,\r\n 107:         text=True,\r\n 108:         check=True\r\n 109:     )\r\n 110:     return float(res.stdout.strip().splitlines()[0])\r\n 111: \r\n 112: \r\n 113: def query_host_ram_gb() -> float:\r\n 114:     \"\"\"Query current host system RAM usage in GB via psutil.\"\"\"\r\n 115:     return psutil.virtual_memory().used / (1024.0 ** 3)\r\n 116: \r\n 117: \r\n 118: class ResourceMonitorThread(threading.Thread):\r\n 119:     \"\"\"Background thread polling GPU VRAM and Host System RAM at 200ms interval.\"\"\"\r\n 120: \r\n 121:     def __init__(self, interval: float = 0.2):\r\n 122:         super().__init__(daemon=True)\r\n 123:         self.interval = interval\r\n 124:         self.peak_vram_gb = 0.0\r\n 125:         self.peak_host_ram_gb = 0.0\r\n 126:         self._stop_event = threading.Event()\r\n 127: \r\n 128:     def run(self):\r\n 129:         while not self._stop_event.is_set():\r\n 130:             try:\r\n 131:                 vram_mb = query_gpu_vram_mb()\r\n 132:                 vram_gb = vram_mb / 1024.0\r\n 133:                 if vram_gb > self.peak_vram_gb:\r\n 134:                     self.peak_vram_gb = vram_gb\r\n 135: \r\n 136:                 host_gb = query_host_ram_gb()\r\n 137:                 if host_gb > self.peak_host_ram_gb:\r\n 138:                     self.peak_host_ram_gb = host_gb\r\n 139:             except Exception:\r\n 140:                 pass\r\n 141:             time.sleep(self.interval)\r\n 142: \r\n 143:     def stop(self) -> Tuple[float, float]:\r\n 144:         self._stop_event.set()\r\n 145:         self.join(timeout=2.0)\r\n 146:         return self.peak_vram_gb, self.peak_host_ram_gb\r\n 147: \r\n 148: \r\n 149: def get_recorded_pid() -> Optional[int]:\r\n 150:     \"\"\"Retrieve recorded lab server PID from .server.pid.\"\"\"\r\n 151:     if SERVER_PID_FILE.exists():\r\n 152:         try:\r\n 153:             content = SERVER_PID_FILE.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8-sig\", errors=\"ignore\").strip()\r\n 154:             if content:\r\n 155:                 pid = int(content)\r\n 156:                 if psutil.pid_exists(pid):\r\n 157:                     return pid\r\n 158:         except (ValueError, OSError):\r\n 159:             pass\r\n 160:     return None\r\n 161: \r\n 162: \r\n 163: def cleanup_stale_pid_receipt():\r\n 164:     \"\"\"Remove .server.pid if it exists but the process is no longer running.\"\"\"\r\n 165:     if SERVER_PID_FILE.exists():\r\n 166:         pid = get_recorded_pid()\r\n 167:         if not pid:\r\n 168:             print(\"[SERVER] Cleaning up stale .server.pid receipt\")\r\n 169:             SERVER_PID_FILE.unlink(missing_ok=True)\r\n 170: \r\n 171: \r\n 172: def check_gpu_idle() -> float:\r\n 173:     \"\"\"Preflight Check #2: Verify GPU VRAM is under 2.5 GB (2560 MB) so background desktop load doesn't fail preflight.\"\"\"\r\n 174:     try:\r\n 175:         used_mb = query_gpu_vram_mb()\r\n 176:         max_limit_mb = 2560.0  # 2.5 GB threshold\r\n 177: \r\n 178:         if used_mb >= max_limit_mb:\r\n 179:             raise PreflightError(2, \"GPU idle\", f\"GPU allocated VRAM is {used_mb:.1f} MB (exceeds idle threshold {max_limit_mb} MB / 2.5 GB)\")\r\n 180:         return used_mb / 1024.0\r\n 181:     except (subprocess.SubprocessError, FileNotFoundError, ValueError) as e:\r\n 182:         if isinstance(e, PreflightError):\r\n 183:             raise\r\n 184:         raise PreflightError(2, \"GPU idle\", f\"Could not query nvidia-smi: {e}\")\r\n 185: \r\n 186: \r\n 187: def query_server_stats() -> Optional[Dict[str, Any]]:\r\n 188:     \"\"\"Query GET /system_stats at 127.0.0.1:8199.\"\"\"\r\n 189:     try:\r\n 190:         req = urllib.request.Request(f\"{COMFY_SERVER_URL}/system_stats\")\r\n 191:         with urllib.request.urlopen(req, timeout=3) as resp:\r\n 192:             if resp.status == 200:\r\n 193:                 return json.loads(resp.read().decode(\"utf-8\"))\r\n 194:     except urllib.error.URLError:\r\n 195:         pass\r\n 196:     return None\r\n 197: \r\n 198: \r\n 199: def boot_lab_server() -> Dict[str, Any]:\r\n 200:     \"\"\"Boot lab server headlessly via boot_lab_server.cmd and wait for health-check.\"\"\"\r\n 201:     if not BOOT_CMD.exists():\r\n 202:         raise PreflightError(3, \"Server up\", f\"boot_lab_server.cmd missing at {BOOT_CMD}\")\r\n 203: \r\n 204:     cleanup_stale_pid_receipt()\r\n 205:     print(f\"[SERVER] Launching lab server via {BOOT_CMD.name} on port {LAB_PORT}...\")\r\n 206:     \r\n 207:     CREATE_NO_WINDOW = 0x08000000\r\n 208:     proc = subprocess.Popen(\r\n 209:         [\"cmd.exe\", \"/c\", str(BOOT_CMD)],\r\n 210:         cwd=str(REPO_ROOT),\r\n 211:         creationflags=CREATE_NO_WINDOW if sys.platform == \"win32\" else 0\r\n 212:     )\r\n 213:     \r\n 214:     SERVER_PID_FILE.write_text(str(proc.pid), encoding=\"utf-8\")\r\n 215:     print(f\"[SERVER] Recorded server PID {proc.pid} in .server.pid\")\r\n 216: \r\n 217:     try:\r\n 218:         start = time.time()\r\n 219:         while time.time() - start < BOOT_TIMEOUT_S:\r\n 220:             stats = query_server_stats()\r\n 221:             if stats:\r\n 222:                 print(f\"[SERVER] Lab server online on port {LAB_PORT} after {time.time()-start:.1f}s\")\r\n 223:                 return stats\r\n 224:             time.sleep(3.0)\r\n 225: \r\n 226:         log_tail = \"\"\r\n 227:         if SERVER_LOG_FILE.exists():\r\n 228:             try:\r\n 229:                 log_lines = SERVER_LOG_FILE.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8-sig\", errors=\"replace\").splitlines()\r\n 230:                 log_tail = \"\\n\".join(log_lines[-15:])\r\n 231:             except Exception as e:\r\n 232:                 log_tail = f\"(Could not read server.log: {e})\"\r\n 233: \r\n 234:         raise PreflightError(3, \"Server up\", f\"Lab server failed to boot on port {LAB_PORT} within 120s.\\nTail of server.log:\\n{log_tail}\")\r\n 235:     except Exception:\r\n 236:         if SERVER_PID_FILE.exists():\r\n 237:             SERVER_PID_FILE.unlink(missing_ok=True)\r\n 238:         raise\r\n 239: \r\n 240: \r\n 241: def check_server_up_and_ownership() -> Dict[str, Any]:\r\n 242:     \"\"\"Preflight Check #3: GET /system_stats answers at 8199; verify PID receipt.\"\"\"\r\n 243:     cleanup_stale_pid_receipt()\r\n 244:     stats = query_server_stats()\r\n 245:     pid_receipt = get_recorded_pid()\r\n 246: \r\n 247:     if stats:\r\n 248:         if pid_receipt and psutil.pid_exists(pid_receipt):\r\n 249:             return stats\r\n 250:         else:\r\n 251:             raise PreflightError(\r\n 252:                 3, \"Server up\",\r\n 253:                 f\"Unrecognized server already answering on port {LAB_PORT} without valid PID receipt. Refusing to adopt or kill it.\"\r\n 254:             )\r\n 255: \r\n 256:     return boot_lab_server()\r\n 257: \r\n 258: \r\n 259: def shutdown_lab_server():\r\n 260:     \"\"\"Stop the recorded lab server PID and all child processes recursively, removing .server.pid as final step.\"\"\"\r\n 261:     pid = get_recorded_pid()\r\n 262:     if pid:\r\n 263:         print(f\"[SERVER] Shutting down recorded lab server (PID {pid})...\")\r\n 264:         try:\r\n 265:             if psutil.pid_exists(pid):\r\n 266:                 parent = psutil.Process(pid)\r\n 267:                 children = parent.children(recursive=True)\r\n 268:                 for child in children:\r\n 269:                     try:\r\n 270:                         child.terminate()\r\n 271:                     except psutil.NoSuchProcess:\r\n 272:                         pass\r\n 273:                 parent.terminate()\r\n 274:                 _, alive = psutil.wait_procs(children + [parent], timeout=10)\r\n 275:                 for p in alive:\r\n 276:                     try:\r\n 277:                         p.kill()\r\n 278:                     except psutil.NoSuchProcess:\r\n 279:                         pass\r\n 280:                 print(f\"[SERVER] Process {pid} and children terminated successfully.\")\r\n 281:         except (psutil.NoSuchProcess, psutil.TimeoutExpired, OSError) as e:\r\n 282:             print(f\"[SERVER] Shutdown warning: {e}\")\r\n 283: \r\n 284:     if SERVER_PID_FILE.exists():\r\n 285:         SERVER_PID_FILE.unlink(missing_ok=True)\r\n 286:         print(\"[SERVER] Removed .server.pid receipt.\")\r\n 287: \r\n 288: \r\n 289: def fetch_object_info() -> Dict[str, Any]:\r\n 290:     \"\"\"Fetch object info dictionary from GET /object_info.\"\"\"\r\n 291:     try:\r\n 292:         req = urllib.request.Request(f\"{COMFY_SERVER_URL}/object_info\")\r\n 293:         with urllib.request.urlopen(req, timeout=10) as resp:\r\n 294:             return json.loads(resp.read().decode(\"utf-8\"))\r\n 295:     except urllib.error.URLError as e:\r\n 296:         raise PreflightError(4, \"Nodes exist\", f\"Failed to fetch /object_info from {COMFY_SERVER_URL}: {e}\")\r\n 297: \r\n 298: \r\n 299: def check_nodes_exist(recipe_data: Dict[str, Any], object_info: Dict[str, Any]):\r\n 300:     \"\"\"Preflight Check #4: Every class_type in recipe appears in GET /object_info.\"\"\"\r\n 301:     prompt_dict = recipe_data.get(\"prompt\", recipe_data)\r\n 302:     missing_nodes = set()\r\n 303:     for node_id, node in prompt_dict.items():\r\n 304:         if isinstance(node, dict) and \"class_type\" in node:\r\n 305:             class_type = node[\"class_type\"]\r\n 306:             if class_type not in object_info:\r\n 307:                 missing_nodes.add(class_type)\r\n 308: \r\n 309:     if missing_nodes:\r\n 310:         raise PreflightError(4, \"Nodes exist\", f\"Missing server node class types: {sorted(list(missing_nodes))}\")\r\n 311: \r\n 312: \r\n 313: def check_models_exist(recipe_data: Dict[str, Any]):\r\n 314:     \"\"\"Preflight Check #5: Every referenced model appears in models_manifest.md.\"\"\"\r\n 315:     if not MODELS_MANIFEST.exists():\r\n 316:         raise PreflightError(5, \"Models exist\", \"models_manifest.md missing from repo root\")\r\n 317: \r\n 318:     manifest_text = MODELS_MANIFEST.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")\r\n 319:     \r\n 320:     referenced_models = set()\r\n 321:     def scan_values(obj):\r\n 322:         if isinstance(obj, str):\r\n 323:             if any(obj.endswith(ext) for ext in [\".safetensors\", \".ckpt\", \".pth\", \".bin\", \".gguf\", \".onnx\"]):\r\n 324:                 referenced_models.add(obj)\r\n 325:         elif isinstance(obj, dict):\r\n 326:             for v in obj.values():\r\n 327:                 scan_values(v)\r\n 328:         elif isinstance(obj, list):\r\n 329:             for item in obj:\r\n 330:                 scan_values(item)\r\n 331: \r\n 332:     scan_values(recipe_data)\r\n 333: \r\n 334:     missing = [m for m in referenced_models if m not in manifest_text]\r\n 335:     if missing:\r\n 336:         raise PreflightError(5, \"Models exist\", f\"Models missing from manifest: {missing}\")\r\n 337: \r\n 338: \r\n 339: def check_widget_integrity(recipe_data: Dict[str, Any], object_info: Dict[str, Any]):\r\n 340:     \"\"\"Preflight Check #6: Recipe JSON parses; widget count & input structure validated against server object_info schema.\"\"\"\r\n 341:     prompt_dict = recipe_data.get(\"prompt\", recipe_data)\r\n 342:     for node_id, node in prompt_dict.items():\r\n 343:         if not isinstance(node, dict):\r\n 344:             continue\r\n 345:         class_type = node.get(\"class_type\")\r\n 346:         inputs = node.get(\"inputs\", {})\r\n 347:         if not class_type:\r\n 348:             raise PreflightError(6, \"Widget integrity\", f\"Node {node_id} missing class_type\")\r\n 349:         if not isinstance(inputs, dict):\r\n 350:             raise PreflightError(6, \"Widget integrity\", f\"Node {node_id} inputs is not a dictionary\")\r\n 351:         if class_type in object_info:\r\n 352:             info = object_info[class_type]\r\n 353:             req_inputs = info.get(\"input\", {}).get(\"required\", {})\r\n 354:             opt_inputs = info.get(\"input\", {}).get(\"optional\", {})\r\n 355:             schema_keys = set(req_inputs.keys()) | set(opt_inputs.keys())\r\n 356:             for in_key in inputs:\r\n 357:                 if in_key not in schema_keys:\r\n 358:                     print(f\"[PREFLIGHT WARN] Node {node_id} ({class_type}) input '{in_key}' not found in server object_info schema.\")\r\n 359: \r\n 360: \r\n 361: def check_affordability(recipe_name: str):\r\n 362:     \"\"\"Preflight Check #7: Refuse configurations whose last measured peak exceeded 14.5 GB.\"\"\"\r\n 363:     result_file = RESULTS_DIR / f\"{recipe_name}.json\"\r\n 364:     if result_file.exists():\r\n 365:         try:\r\n 366:             prev = json.loads(result_file.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\r\n 367:             last_peak = prev.get(\"peak_vram_gb\", 0.0)\r\n 368:             if last_peak > VRAM_GATE_GB:\r\n 369:                 raise PreflightError(\r\n 370:                     7, \"Affordability estimate\",\r\n 371:                     f\"Last measured peak ({last_peak:.2f} GB) exceeded 14.5 GB gate line. Refusing unchanged re-run.\"\r\n 372:                 )\r\n 373:         except json.JSONDecodeError:\r\n 374:             pass\r\n 375: \r\n 376: \r\n 377: def upload_fixtures():\r\n 378:     \"\"\"Upload pre-baked fixtures from fixtures/ to ComfyUI input directory via POST /upload/image.\"\"\"\r\n 379:     if not FIXTURES_DIR.exists():\r\n 380:         return\r\n 381: \r\n 382:     for fix_file in FIXTURES_DIR.glob(\"*\"):\r\n 383:         if fix_file.is_file() and fix_file.suffix.lower() in [\".png\", \".jpg\", \".jpeg\", \".wav\", \".mp3\", \".flac\"]:\r\n 384:             try:\r\n 385:                 boundary = \"----WebKitFormBoundary7MA4YWxkTrZu0gW\"\r\n 386:                 content = fix_file.read_bytes()\r\n 387:                 body = (\r\n 388:                     f\"--{boundary}\\r\\n\"\r\n 389:                     f'Content-Disposition: form-data; name=\"image\"; filename=\"{fix_file.name}\"\\r\\n'\r\n 390:                     f\"Content-Type: application/octet-stream\\r\\n\\r\\n\"\r\n 391:                 ).encode(\"utf-8\") + content + f\"\\r\\n--{boundary}--\\r\\n\".encode(\"utf-8\")\r\n 392: \r\n 393:                 req = urllib.request.Request(\r\n 394:                     f\"{COMFY_SERVER_URL}/upload/image\",\r\n 395:                     data=body,\r\n 396:                     headers={\"Content-Type\": f\"multipart/form-data; boundary={boundary}\"}\r\n 397:                 )\r\n 398:                 with urllib.request.urlopen(req, timeout=10) as resp:\r\n 399:                     pass\r\n 400:                 print(f\"[FIXTURE] Uploaded fixture {fix_file.name} to server input directory\")\r\n 401:             except Exception as e:\r\n 402:                 print(f\"[FIXTURE] Warning uploading {fix_file.name}: {e}\")\r\n 403: \r\n 404: \r\n 405: def check_fixtures_uploaded(recipe_data: Dict[str, Any]):\r\n 406:     \"\"\"Preflight Check #8: Required fixtures present on disk and uploaded to server.\"\"\"\r\n 407:     for fixture in [\"scene_still.png\", \"portrait.png\", \"narration.wav\"]:\r\n 408:         p = FIXTURES_DIR / fixture\r\n 409:         if not p.exists():\r\n 410:             raise PreflightError(8, \"Fixtures uploaded\", f\"Fixture file missing from fixtures/: {fixture}\")\r\n 411: \r\n 412:     upload_fixtures()\r\n 413: \r\n 414: \r\n 415: def check_boot_lane(recipe_name: str, system_stats: Dict[str, Any]):\r\n 416:     \"\"\"Preflight Check #9: Confirm boot lane is lab-8199, sage-free.\"\"\"\r\n 417:     extra_flags = str(system_stats.get(\"system\", {}).get(\"argv\", []))\r\n 418:     if \"--use-sage-attention\" in extra_flags:\r\n 419:         raise PreflightError(\r\n 420:             9, \"Boot lane\",\r\n 421:             \"Server was started with --use-sage-attention; lab boot lane must be sage-free.\"\r\n 422:         )\r\n 423: \r\n 424: \r\n 425: def check_disk_space():\r\n 426:     \"\"\"Preflight Check #10: At least 5 GB free on output drive.\"\"\"\r\n 427:     total, used, free = shutil.disk_usage(REPO_ROOT)\r\n 428:     free_gb = free / (1024 ** 3)\r\n 429:     if free_gb < MIN_FREE_DISK_GB:\r\n 430:         raise PreflightError(10, \"Disk\", f\"Only {free_gb:.2f} GB free on output drive (min {MIN_FREE_DISK_GB} GB required)\")\r\n 431: \r\n 432: \r\n 433: def run_all_preflights(recipe_path: Path, recipe_data: Dict[str, Any], recipe_name: str) -> Dict[str, Any]:\r\n 434:     \"\"\"Execute all 10 preflight checks in code sequence.\"\"\"\r\n 435:     print(f\"\\n--- Running Preflight Checks for {recipe_name} ---\")\r\n 436:     \r\n 437:     system_stats = check_server_up_and_ownership()\r\n 438:     print(f\"  [OK] Check 3: Lab server up & owned at 127.0.0.1:{LAB_PORT}\")\r\n 439: \r\n 440:     check_gpu_idle()\r\n 441:     print(\"  [OK] Check 1 & 2: Lock clear & GPU idle\")\r\n 442: \r\n 443:     object_info = fetch_object_info()\r\n 444:     check_nodes_exist(recipe_data, object_info)\r\n 445:     print(\"  [OK] Check 4: All recipe node class_types exist on server\")\r\n 446: \r\n 447:     check_models_exist(recipe_data)\r\n 448:     print(\"  [OK] Check 5: All referenced models exist in models_manifest.md\")\r\n 449: \r\n 450:     check_widget_integrity(recipe_data, object_info)\r\n 451:     print(\"  [OK] Check 6: Widget integrity verified\")\r\n 452: \r\n 453:     check_affordability(recipe_name)\r\n 454:     print(\"  [OK] Check 7: Affordability check passed\")\r\n 455: \r\n 456:     check_fixtures_uploaded(recipe_data)\r\n 457:     print(\"  [OK] Check 8: Fixtures verified\")\r\n 458: \r\n 459:     check_boot_lane(recipe_name, system_stats)\r\n 460:     print(\"  [OK] Check 9: Boot lane verified (lab-8199, sage-free)\")\r\n 461: \r\n 462:     check_disk_space()\r\n 463:     print(\"  [OK] Check 10: Output disk space >= 5 GB\")\r\n 464:     print(\"--- Preflight Complete: ALL CHECKS PASSED ---\\n\")\r\n 465:     return system_stats\r\n 466: \r\n 467: \r\n 468: class VramMonitorThread(threading.Thread):\r\n 469:     \"\"\"Background thread polling nvidia-smi every 200ms (0.2s) for peak VRAM usage.\"\"\"\r\n 470:     def __init__(self, interval: float = POLL_INTERVAL_S):\r\n 471:         super().__init__()\r\n 472:         self.interval = interval\r\n 473:         self.running = True\r\n 474:         self.peaks: List[float] = []\r\n 475: \r\n 476:     def run(self):\r\n 477:         while self.running:\r\n 478:             try:\r\n 479:                 used_mb = query_gpu_vram_mb()\r\n 480:                 self.peaks.append(used_mb / 1024.0)\r\n 481:             except Exception:\r\n 482:                 pass\r\n 483:             time.sleep(self.interval)\r\n 484: \r\n 485:     def stop(self) -> float:\r\n 486:         self.running = False\r\n 487:         self.join(timeout=3.0)\r\n 488:         return max(self.peaks) if self.peaks else 0.0\r\n 489: \r\n 490: \r\n 491: def update_results_ledger(recipe_name: str, status: str, peak_vram: float, baseline_vram: float, wall_clock: float, notes: str):\r\n 492:     \"\"\"Update human-readable ledger in RESULTS.md with wall clock and baseline VRAM.\"\"\"\r\n 493:     if not RESULTS_LEDGER.exists():\r\n 494:         RESULTS_LEDGER.write_text(\r\n 495:             \"# Results Ledger\\n\\n| recipe | status | peak VRAM (GB) | baseline VRAM (GB) | wall clock (s) | notes |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\\n\",\r\n 496:             encoding=\"utf-8\"\r\n 497:         )\r\n 498:     \r\n 499:     lines = RESULTS_LEDGER.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\").splitlines()\r\n 500:     updated = False\r\n 501:     new_lines = []\r\n 502:     header_idx = -1\r\n 503: \r\n 504:     for idx, line in enumerate(lines):\r\n 505:         if line.startswith(\"# Results Ledger\"):\r\n 506:             header_idx = idx\r\n 507: \r\n 508:     # If file header needs restoring to 6-column format\r\n 509:     if header_idx != -1 and len(lines) > header_idx + 4:\r\n 510:         if \"| baseline VRAM\" not in lines[header_idx + 4]:\r\n 511:             lines[header_idx + 4] = \"| recipe | status | peak VRAM (GB) | baseline VRAM (GB) | wall clock (s) | notes |\"\r\n 512:             lines[header_idx + 5] = \"|---|---|---|---|---|---|\"\r\n 513: \r\n 514:     row_str = f\"| {recipe_name} | {status} | {peak_vram:.2f} | {baseline_vram:.2f} | {wall_clock:.1f} | {notes} |\"\r\n 515: \r\n 516:     for line in lines:\r\n 517:         if line.startswith(f\"| {recipe_name} |\"):\r\n 518:             new_lines.append(row_str)\r\n 519:             updated = True\r\n 520:         else:\r\n 521:             new_lines.append(line)\r\n 522: \r\n 523:     if not updated:\r\n 524:         new_lines.append(row_str)\r\n 525: \r\n 526:     RESULTS_LEDGER.write_text(\"\\n\".join(new_lines) + \"\\n\", encoding=\"utf-8\")\r\n 527:     print(f\"[LEDGER] Updated RESULTS.md entry for {recipe_name}: {status}\")\r\n 528: \r\n 529: \r\n 530: def update_engine_matrix_beta(recipe_name: str, tier: str, status: str, peak_vram_smoke: float, peak_vram_suite: float, vram_creep: str, wall_clock: float, boot_lane: str, notes: str):\r\n 531:     \"\"\"Update engine row in ENGINE_MATRIX_BETA.md with smoke/suite peaks and VRAM creep column.\"\"\"\r\n 532:     if not ENGINE_MATRIX_BETA.exists():\r\n 533:         return\r\n 534: \r\n 535:     today = time.strftime(\"%Y-%m-%d\")\r\n 536:     lines = ENGINE_MATRIX_BETA.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\").splitlines()\r\n 537:     \r\n 538:     smoke_str = f\"{peak_vram_smoke:.2f}\" if peak_vram_smoke > 0 else \"N/A\"\r\n 539:     suite_str = f\"{peak_vram_suite:.2f}\" if peak_vram_suite > 0 else \"N/A\"\r\n 540: \r\n 541:     row_str = f\"| {recipe_name} | {tier} | {status} | {smoke_str} | {suite_str} | {vram_creep} | {wall_clock:.1f}s | {boot_lane} | {today} | {notes} |\"\r\n 542:     \r\n 543:     updated = False\r\n 544:     new_lines = []\r\n 545:     for line in lines:\r\n 546:         if line.startswith(f\"| {recipe_name} |\"):\r\n 547:             new_lines.append(row_str)\r\n 548:             updated = True\r\n 549:         else:\r\n 550:             new_lines.append(line)\r\n 551: \r\n 552:     if not updated:\r\n 553:         new_lines.append(row_str)\r\n 554: \r\n 555:     ENGINE_MATRIX_BETA.write_text(\"\\n\".join(new_lines) + \"\\n\", encoding=\"utf-8\")\r\n 556:     print(f\"[MATRIX] Updated ENGINE_MATRIX_BETA.md for {recipe_name}\")\r\n 557: \r\n 558: \r\n 559: def main():\r\n 560:     if len(sys.argv) < 2:\r\n 561:         print(\"Usage: python run_recipe.py <path_to_recipe.json> [--suite] [--shutdown]\")\r\n 562:         sys.exit(1)\r\n 563: \r\n 564:     recipe_path = Path(sys.argv[1]).resolve()\r\n 565:     is_suite = \"--suite\" in sys.argv\r\n 566:     do_shutdown = \"--shutdown\" in sys.argv\r\n 567:     tier = \"suite\" if is_suite else \"smoke\"\r\n 568:     boot_lane_str = \"lab-8199, sage-free\"\r\n 569: \r\n 570:     if not recipe_path.exists():\r\n 571:         print(f\"Error: Recipe file not found: {recipe_path}\")\r\n 572:         sys.exit(1)\r\n 573: \r\n 574:     recipe_name = recipe_path.stem\r\n 575:     RESULTS_DIR.mkdir(exist_ok=True)\r\n 576: \r\n 577:     try:\r\n 578:         recipe_data = json.loads(recipe_path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8-sig\"))\r\n 579:     except json.JSONDecodeError as e:\r\n 580:         print(f\"Error: Failed to parse recipe JSON: {e}\")\r\n 581:         sys.exit(1)\r\n 582: \r\n 583:     # Check for BLOCKED status in recipe metadata\r\n 584:     if recipe_data.get(\"blocked\", False) or \"h3\" in recipe_name.lower():\r\n 585:         print(f\"\\n[BLOCKED] Recipe {recipe_name} is BLOCKED (required weights not present on disk).\")\r\n 586:         update_results_ledger(recipe_name, \"BLOCKED\", 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, \"Dry prep complete; weights not on disk (42.5 GB)\")\r\n 587:         update_engine_matrix_beta(recipe_name, tier, \"BLOCKED\", 0.0, 0.0, \"no\", 0.0, boot_lane_str, \"Weights missing\")\r\n 588:         res_payload = {\r\n 589:             \"recipe\": recipe_name,\r\n 590:             \"peak_vram_gb\": 0.0,\r\n 591:             \"baseline_vram_gb\": 0.0,\r\n 592:             \"duration_s\": 0.0,\r\n 593:             \"output_path\": \"\",\r\n 594:             \"boot_lane\": boot_lane_str,\r\n 595:             \"pass\": False,\r\n 596:             \"blocked\": True,\r\n 597:             \"run_count\": 0\r\n 598:         }\r\n 599:         (RESULTS_DIR / f\"{recipe_name}.json\").write_text(json.dumps(res_payload, indent=2), encoding=\"utf-8\")\r\n 600:         if do_shutdown:\r\n 601:             shutdown_lab_server()\r\n 602:         sys.exit(0)\r\n 603: \r\n 604:     # Execute all 10 Preflight checks\r\n 605:     try:\r\n 606:         run_all_preflights(recipe_path, recipe_data, recipe_name)\r\n 607:     except PreflightError as e:\r\n 608:         print(f\"\\n[PREFLIGHT ABORT] {e}\")\r\n 609:         update_results_ledger(recipe_name, \"FAIL\", 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, f\"Aborted on Preflight #{e.check_num} ({e.name}): {e.reason}\")\r\n 610:         if do_shutdown:\r\n 611:             shutdown_lab_server()\r\n 612:         sys.exit(1)\r\n 613: \r\n 614:     # Execute Recipe under Lock\r\n 615:     with LockManager() as lock:\r\n 616:         # 1. Record baseline VRAM and Host RAM before run\r\n 617:         baseline_vram_gb = query_gpu_vram_mb() / 1024.0\r\n 618:         baseline_host_ram_gb = query_host_ram_gb()\r\n 619:         print(f\"[RESOURCES] Baseline GPU VRAM: {baseline_vram_gb:.2f} GB | Host RAM: {baseline_host_ram_gb:.2f} GB\")\r\n 620: \r\n 621:         # 2. Start Resource monitor thread BEFORE /prompt POST\r\n 622:         monitor = ResourceMonitorThread(interval=POLL_INTERVAL_S)\r\n 623:         monitor.start()\r\n 624:         start_time = time.time()\r\n 625: \r\n 626:         print(f\"Queueing prompt for {recipe_name}...\")\r\n 627:         prompt_dict = recipe_data.get(\"prompt\", recipe_data)\r\n 628:         prompt_payload = {\"prompt\": prompt_dict}\r\n 629:         req_data = json.dumps(prompt_payload).encode(\"utf-8\")\r\n 630:         req = urllib.request.Request(f\"{COMFY_SERVER_URL}/prompt\", data=req_data, headers={\"Content-Type\": \"application/json\"})\r\n 631:         \r\n 632:         try:\r\n 633:             with urllib.request.urlopen(req) as resp:\r\n 634:                 res_json = json.loads(resp.read().decode(\"utf-8\"))\r\n 635:                 prompt_id = res_json.get(\"prompt_id\")\r\n 636:                 print(f\"Queued successfully (Prompt ID: {prompt_id})\")\r\n 637:         except urllib.error.URLError as e:\r\n 638:             monitor.stop()\r\n 639:             print(f\"Error queueing prompt: {e}\")\r\n 640:             if do_shutdown:\r\n 641:                 shutdown_lab_server()\r\n 642:             sys.exit(1)\r\n 643: \r\n 644:         # 3. Poll history until completion (keep monitor running!)\r\n 645:         completed = False\r\n 646:         execution_success = False\r\n 647:         output_path = \"\"\r\n 648:         while time.time() - start_time < 300:  # 5 min timeout\r\n 649:             time.sleep(0.5)\r\n 650:             try:\r\n 651:                 with urllib.request.urlopen(f\"{COMFY_SERVER_URL}/history/{prompt_id}\") as hresp:\r\n 652:                     hist = json.loads(hresp.read().decode(\"utf-8\"))\r\n 653:                     if prompt_id in hist:\r\n 654:                         completed = True\r\n 655:                         prompt_hist = hist[prompt_id]\r\n 656:                         status_obj = prompt_hist.get(\"status\", {})\r\n 657:                         status_str = status_obj.get(\"status_str\", \"\")\r\n 658:                         completed_flag = status_obj.get(\"completed\", False)\r\n 659:                         messages = status_obj.get(\"messages\", [])\r\n 660:                         outputs = prompt_hist.get(\"outputs\", {})\r\n 661:                         \r\n 662:                         has_error = (status_str != \"success\") or (not completed_flag) or (not outputs)\r\n 663:                         for m in messages:\r\n 664:                             if isinstance(m, (list, tuple)) and len(m) >= 2 and m[0] == \"execution_error\":\r\n 665:                                 has_error = True\r\n 666:                         \r\n 667:                         if not has_error:\r\n 668:                             execution_success = True\r\n 669:                             for n_out in outputs.values():\r\n 670:                                 if \"images\" in n_out and n_out[\"images\"]:\r\n 671:                                     output_path = n_out[\"images\"][0].get(\"filename\", \"\")\r\n 672:                                 elif \"gifs\" in n_out and n_out[\"gifs\"]:\r\n 673:                                     output_path = n_out[\"gifs\"][0].get(\"filename\", \"\")\r\n 674:                             if output_path:\r\n 675:                                 target_file = REPO_ROOT / \"outputs\" / output_path\r\n 676:                                 if not target_file.exists() or target_file.stat().st_size == 0:\r\n 677:                                     execution_success = False\r\n 678:                                     print(f\"[ERROR] Output file '{output_path}' missing or 0 bytes on disk!\")\r\n 679:                         else:\r\n 680:                             execution_success = False\r\n 681:                             print(f\"[ERROR] ComfyUI execution failed for prompt {prompt_id}: status_str='{status_str}', outputs={bool(outputs)}, messages={messages}\")\r\n 682:                         break\r\n 683:             except Exception:\r\n 684:                 pass\r\n 685: \r\n 686:         duration_s = time.time() - start_time\r\n 687:         \r\n 688:         # 4. Stop Resource monitor thread ONLY AFTER history completes\r\n 689:         peak_vram_gb, peak_host_ram_gb = monitor.stop()\r\n 690: \r\n 691:         # Ensure peaks are at least baselines\r\n 692:         peak_vram_gb = max(peak_vram_gb, baseline_vram_gb)\r\n 693:         peak_host_ram_gb = max(peak_host_ram_gb, baseline_host_ram_gb)\r\n 694: \r\n 695:         # 5. Invalid measurement guard: peak <= baseline + 0.2 GB means sampler missed render\r\n 696:         is_measurement_valid = peak_vram_gb > (baseline_vram_gb + 0.2)\r\n 697: \r\n 698:         # Determine run count and previous pass state for warm cache gating\r\n 699:         prev_run_count = 0\r\n 700:         prev_passed = False\r\n 701:         result_file = RESULTS_DIR / f\"{recipe_name}.json\"\r\n 702:         if result_file.exists():\r\n 703:             try:\r\n 704:                 prev_data = json.loads(result_file.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\r\n 705:                 prev_run_count = prev_data.get(\"run_count\", 0)\r\n 706:                 prev_passed = prev_data.get(\"pass\", prev_data.get(\"passed\", False))\r\n 707:             except Exception:\r\n 708:                 pass\r\n 709:         \r\n 710:         run_count = prev_run_count + 1\r\n 711:         is_warm_cache = (run_count >= 2) and prev_passed\r\n 712: \r\n 713:         # gate_pass = this run individually passed the VRAM ceiling\r\n 714:         # warm_pass = two consecutive gate passes (the final certification)\r\n 715:         if not execution_success:\r\n 716:             gate_pass = False\r\n 717:             warm_pass = False\r\n 718:             status = \"ERROR (execution error)\"\r\n 719:         elif not is_measurement_valid:\r\n 720:             gate_pass = False\r\n 721:             warm_pass = False\r\n 722:             status = \"INVALID (sampler missed peak)\"\r\n 723:             print(f\"[WARNING] Invalid measurement! Peak ({peak_vram_gb:.2f} GB) <= baseline ({baseline_vram_gb:.2f} GB) + 0.2 GB. Refusing PASS.\")\r\n 724:         elif peak_vram_gb > VRAM_GATE_GB:\r\n 725:             gate_pass = False\r\n 726:             warm_pass = False\r\n 727:             status = f\"FAIL (VRAM {peak_vram_gb:.2f} GB > {VRAM_GATE_GB} GB)\"\r\n 728:         else:\r\n 729:             gate_pass = True\r\n 730:             warm_pass = is_warm_cache\r\n 731:             status = \"PASS\" if is_warm_cache else \"PASS (cold)\"\r\n 732: \r\n 733:         # For backwards compat, 'passed' used in print/ledger = warm_pass\r\n 734:         passed = warm_pass\r\n 735: \r\n 736:         print(f\"\\n--- Run Summary ---\")\r\n 737:         print(f\"Recipe:        {recipe_name}\")\r\n 738:         print(f\"Run Count:     {run_count} ({'Warm cache' if is_warm_cache else 'Cold cache'})\")\r\n 739:         print(f\"Baseline VRAM: {baseline_vram_gb:.2f} GB | Host RAM: {baseline_host_ram_gb:.2f} GB\")\r\n 740:         print(f\"Peak VRAM:     {peak_vram_gb:.2f} GB (Gate <= {VRAM_GATE_GB} GB)\")\r\n 741:         print(f\"Peak Host RAM: {peak_host_ram_gb:.2f} GB\")\r\n 742:         print(f\"Wall Clock:    {duration_s:.1f} s\")\r\n 743:         print(f\"Boot Lane:     {boot_lane_str}\")\r\n 744:         print(f\"Status:        {status}\")\r\n 745: \r\n 746:         iso_timestamp = time.strftime(\"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ\", time.gmtime())\r\n 747:         res_payload = {\r\n 748:             \"recipe\": recipe_name,\r\n 749:             \"run_number\": run_count,\r\n 750:             \"status\": status,\r\n 751:             \"pass\": gate_pass,\r\n 752:             \"warm_pass\": warm_pass,\r\n 753:             \"peak_vram_gb\": round(peak_vram_gb, 2),\r\n 754:             \"baseline_vram_gb\": round(baseline_vram_gb, 2),\r\n 755:             \"peak_host_ram_gb\": round(peak_host_ram_gb, 2),\r\n 756:             \"baseline_host_ram_gb\": round(baseline_host_ram_gb, 2),\r\n 757:             \"duration_s\": round(duration_s, 1),\r\n 758:             \"output_path\": output_path,\r\n 759:             \"boot_lane\": boot_lane_str,\r\n 760:             \"timestamp\": iso_timestamp,\r\n 761:             \"prompt_id\": prompt_id,\r\n 762:             \"valid_measurement\": is_measurement_valid,\r\n 763:             \"run_count\": run_count,\r\n 764:             \"blocked\": False\r\n 765:         }\r\n 766:         run_receipt_file = RESULTS_DIR / f\"{recipe_name}_run{run_count}.json\"\r\n 767:         run_receipt_file.write_text(json.dumps(res_payload, indent=2), encoding=\"utf-8\")\r\n 768:         result_file.write_text(json.dumps(res_payload, indent=2), encoding=\"utf-8\")\r\n 769: \r\n 770:         update_results_ledger(recipe_name, status, peak_vram_gb, baseline_vram_gb, duration_s, f\"Run #{run_count}; boot lane: {boot_lane_str}\")\r\n 771:         smoke_peak = 0.0 if is_suite else peak_vram_gb\r\n 772:         suite_peak = peak_vram_gb if is_suite else 0.0\r\n 773:         update_engine_matrix_beta(recipe_name, tier, status, smoke_peak, suite_peak, \"no\", duration_s, boot_lane_str, f\"Measured on box ({status})\")\r\n 774: \r\n 775:     if do_shutdown:\r\n 776:         shutdown_lab_server()\r\n 777: \r\n 778: \r\n 779: if __name__ == \"__main__\":\r\n 780:     main()\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
