\"server did not come up\").\r\n  27: - **Sage-free by construction:** the boot passes no `--use-sage-attention`.\r\n  28:   This satisfies PREFLIGHT check 9 for MiniMax H3 automatically. If a recipe\r\n  29:   ever needs Sage, that is a per-workflow setting, not a boot flag.\r\n  30: \r\n  31: ## Health check (before any queue)\r\n  32: \r\n  33: Poll `GET http://127.0.0.1:8199/system_stats` every 3 s, up to 120 s. First\r\n  34: 200 response = server up. On timeout, read the tail of `server.log` (repo\r\n  35: root, append-mode) and report the actual error ƒ?\" do not just retry.\r\n  36: \r\n  37: ## Shutdown\r\n  38: \r\n  39: Stop the recorded PID (`Stop-Process -Id <pid>`), then confirm the port no\r\n  40: longer answers. Always shut down a server you booted when the session's runs\r\n  41: are done ƒ?\" an idle loaded server holds VRAM that the next preflight's\r\n  42: GPU-idle check (under 1.5 GB) will refuse.\r\n  43: \r\n  44: ## Rules\r\n  45: \r\n  46: - ONE lab server at a time; the `.gpu.lock` discipline applies to booting too.\r\n  47: - Never kill a ComfyUI process the lab did not start (PID receipt or leave it).\r\n  48: - If port 8199 is already answering and no lab PID is recorded, something else\r\n  49:   owns it: abort and report, do not adopt it and do not kill it.\r\n  50: - `outputs/` and `server.log` are runtime artifacts: gitignored, never\r\n  51:   committed, safe to clean between sessions.\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_26","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\WINDOWS\\\\System32\\\\WindowsPowerShell\\\\v1.0\\\\powershell.exe\" -Command '$i=0; Get-Content -LiteralPath '\"'validate_recipes.py' | ForEach-Object { \"'$i++; '\"'{0,4}: {1}' -f \"'$i, $_ }'","aggregated_output":"   1: #!/usr/bin/env python3\r\n   2: \"\"\"\r\n   3: Offline Paper Validation Script for vram-recipe-lab recipes.\r\n   4: Runs all static validations that do NOT require a live lab server:\r\n   5:   1. Strict UTF-8 encoding (NO BOM)\r\n   6:   2. JSON parsing validity\r\n   7:   3. Recipe contract integrity (width, height, frames, vram_ceiling_gb)\r\n   8:   4. Mandatory coverage of all 16 canonical recipes\r\n   9:   5. Node class_type presence and prompt dictionary structure\r\n  10:   6. Graph reachability, link index integrity, and data types\r\n  11:   7. Sink output node type validation (SaveImage for still, SaveVideo for video)\r\n  12:   8. Fixture file existence for I2V/R2V/Audio recipes\r\n  13: \"\"\"\r\n  14: \r\n  15: import json\r\n  16: import sys\r\n  17: from pathlib import Path\r\n  18: \r\n  19: REPO_ROOT = Path(__file__).parent.resolve()\r\n  20: RECIPES_DIR = REPO_ROOT / \"recipes\"\r\n  21: FIXTURES_DIR = REPO_ROOT / \"fixtures\"\r\n  22: \r\n  23: REQUIRED_RECIPES = [\r\n  24:     \"t2i_low\", \"t2i_high\",\r\n  25:     \"wan_ti2v_low\", \"wan_ti2v_high\",\r\n  26:     \"wan_i2v_14b_low\", \"wan_i2v_14b_high\",\r\n  27:     \"ltx_i2v_low\", \"ltx_i2v_high\",\r\n  28:     \"ltx_audio_low\", \"ltx_lipsync_low\",\r\n  29:     \"h3_t2v_low\", \"h3_t2v_best\",\r\n  30:     \"h3_i2v_low\", \"h3_i2v_best\",\r\n  31:     \"h3_r2v_low\", \"h3_r2v_best\"\r\n  32: ]\r\n  33: \r\n  34: \r\n  35: def validate_recipe_file(recipe_path: Path) -> dict:\r\n  36:     recipe_name = recipe_path.stem\r\n  37:     errors = []\r\n  38:     warnings = []\r\n  39: \r\n  40:     # 1. Check UTF-8 (Strict NO BOM)\r\n  41:     raw_bytes = recipe_path.read_bytes()\r\n  42:     if raw_bytes.startswith(b\"\\xef\\xbb\\xbf\"):\r\n  43:         errors.append(\"UTF-8 BOM detected at start of file (must be UTF-8 without BOM)\")\r\n  44: \r\n  45:     # 2. Parse JSON\r\n  46:     try:\r\n  47:         content = raw_bytes.decode(\"utf-8\")\r\n  48:         data = json.loads(content)\r\n  49:     except Exception as e:\r\n  50:         return {\"recipe\": recipe_name, \"valid\": False, \"errors\": [f\"JSON parse error: {e}\"], \"warnings\": []}\r\n  51: \r\n  52:     # 3. Check top-level contract keys\r\n  53:     if \"name\" not in data or data[\"name\"] != recipe_name:\r\n  54:         errors.append(f\"Name mismatch: expected '{recipe_name}', got '{data.get('name')}'\")\r\n  55:     if \"contract\" not in data or not isinstance(data[\"contract\"], dict):\r\n  56:         errors.append(\"Missing or invalid 'contract' dictionary\")\r\n  57:     else:\r\n  58:         contract = data[\"contract\"]\r\n  59:         for field in [\"width\", \"height\", \"vram_ceiling_gb\"]:\r\n  60:             if field not in contract:\r\n  61:                 errors.append(f\"Missing contract field: {field}\")\r\n  62:         if \"t2i\" not in recipe_name and \"frames\" not in contract:\r\n  63:             errors.append(\"Missing contract field: frames\")\r\n  64: \r\n  65:     # 4. Check prompt structure & graph topology\r\n  66:     prompt = data.get(\"prompt\", {})\r\n  67:     if not isinstance(prompt, dict) or not prompt:\r\n  68:         errors.append(\"Missing or empty 'prompt' dictionary\")\r\n  69:     else:\r\n  70:         node_ids = set(prompt.keys())\r\n  71:         has_video_save = False\r\n  72:         has_image_save = False\r\n  73: \r\n  74:         for node_id, node in prompt.items():\r\n  75:             if not isinstance(node, dict):\r\n  76:                 errors.append(f\"Node {node_id} is not a dictionary\")\r\n  77:                 continue\r\n  78:             class_type = node.get(\"class_type\")\r\n  79:             if not class_type:\r\n  80:                 errors.append(f\"Node {node_id} missing 'class_type'\")\r\n  81:                 continue\r\n  82: \r\n  83:             if class_type == \"SaveVideo\":\r\n  84:                 has_video_save = True\r\n  85:             elif class_type == \"SaveImage\":\r\n  86:                 has_image_save = True\r\n  87: \r\n  88:             inputs = node.get(\"inputs\", {})\r\n  89:             if not isinstance(inputs, dict):\r\n  90:                 errors.append(f\"Node {node_id} 'inputs' is not a dictionary\")\r\n  91:                 continue\r\n  92: \r\n  93:             # 5. Check links & graph reachability\r\n  94:             for in_key, in_val in inputs.items():\r\n  95:                 if isinstance(in_val, list) and len(in_val) == 2:\r\n  96:                     target_id, slot_idx = str(in_val[0]), in_val[1]\r\n  97:                     if target_id not in node_ids:\r\n  98:                         errors.append(f\"Node {node_id} input '{in_key}' references non-existent node {target_id}\")\r\n  99: \r\n 100:         # 6. Check sink output node type match\r\n 101:         if \"t2i\" in recipe_name:\r\n 102:             if not has_image_save:\r\n 103:                 errors.append(\"Still image recipe missing SaveImage sink node\")\r\n 104:         else:\r\n 105:             if not has_video_save:\r\n 106:                 errors.append(\"Video recipe missing SaveVideo sink node (must end in SaveVideo)\")\r\n 107: \r\n 108:     # 7. Check fixtures for image/audio recipes\r\n 109:     if \"i2v\" in recipe_name or \"r2v\" in recipe_name:\r\n 110:         fixture_name = \"portrait.png\" if \"r2v\" in recipe_name else \"scene_still.png\"\r\n 111:         p = FIXTURES_DIR / fixture_name\r\n 112:         if not p.exists():\r\n 113:             warnings.append(f\"Fixture file missing: {fixture_name}\")\r\n 114: \r\n 115:     if \"audio\" in recipe_name:\r\n 116:         p = FIXTURES_DIR / \"narration.wav\"\r\n 117:         if not p.exists():\r\n 118:             warnings.append(f\"Fixture file missing: narration.wav\")\r\n 119: \r\n 120:     return {\r\n 121:         \"recipe\": recipe_name,\r\n 122:         \"valid\": len(errors) == 0,\r\n 123:         \"errors\": errors,\r\n 124:         \"warnings\": warnings,\r\n 125:         \"node_count\": len(prompt) if isinstance(prompt, dict) else 0,\r\n 126:         \"blocked\": data.get(\"blocked\", False)\r\n 127:     }\r\n 128: \r\n 129: \r\n 130: def main():\r\n 131:     print(\"=========================================================\")\r\n 132:     print(\"       vram-recipe-lab :: PAPER VALIDATION SUITE        \")\r\n 133:     print(\"=========================================================\\n\")\r\n 134: \r\n 135:     results = []\r\n 136:     all_valid = True\r\n 137: \r\n 138:     for recipe_name in REQUIRED_RECIPES:\r\n 139:         recipe_path = RECIPES_DIR / f\"{recipe_name}.json\"\r\n 140:         if not recipe_path.exists():\r\n 141:             print(f\"[MISSING] Required recipe file missing: {recipe_name}.json!\")\r\n 142:             all_valid = False\r\n 143:             continue\r\n 144: \r\n 145:         res = validate_recipe_file(recipe_path)\r\n 146:         results.append(res)\r\n 147: \r\n 148:         status_str = \"PASS\" if res[\"valid\"] else \"FAIL\"\r\n 149:         blocked_str = \"[BLOCKED]\" if res[\"blocked\"] else \"[ACTIVE]\"\r\n 150:         print(f\"  {status_str:4s} | {blocked_str:9s} | {recipe_name:20s} ({res['node_count']} nodes)\")\r\n 151:         for err in res[\"errors\"]:\r\n 152:             print(f\"         +-- ERROR: {err}\")\r\n 153:         for warn in res[\"warnings\"]:\r\n 154:             print(f\"         +-- WARN:  {warn}\")\r\n 155: \r\n 156:     print(\"\\n---------------------------------------------------------\")\r\n 157:     passed_count = sum(1 for r in results if r[\"valid\"])\r\n 158:     total_count = len(REQUIRED_RECIPES)\r\n 159:     print(f\"Summary: {passed_count}/{total_count} required recipes PAPER VALIDATED successfully.\")\r\n 160:     print(\"Note: Schema-vs-/object_info live server checks marked PENDING server window.\")\r\n 161:     print(\"=========================================================\\n\")\r\n 162: \r\n 163:     if passed_count != total_count or len(results) != total_count:\r\n 164:         sys.exit(1)\r\n 165: \r\n 166: \r\n 167: if __name__ == \"__main__\":\r\n 168:     main()\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_27","type":"agent_message","text":"VERDICT: no. The document is a diagnostic prompt, not a build-ready plan; it skips graph correctness, receipt integrity, and re-test policy.\n\nMUST-FIX BEFORE BUILD:\n1. [Issue 1, lines 19-21] The LTX diagnosis targets `CLIPTextEncode` / `LTXVConditioning`, but the actual recipes do not contain `LTXVConditioning` and do not connect `LoadImage` at all. In `recipes/ltx_i2v_low.json`, `LoadImage` is node 4 at lines 35-39, but `KSampler` only consumes model/text/empty latent at lines 78-93; `recipes/ltx_i2v_high.json` has the same structure at lines 35-39 and 78-93. Concrete fix: rewrite Issue 1 as a graph-repair task first: define the intended LTXV/LTXAV node chain, image-conditioning path, and connector/embedding model path before investigating tensor dimensions.\n\n2. [Issue 1, lines 10-21] The document treats the runtime error as an encoder-dimension mystery, but the repo already records a stronger hypothesis: `models_manifest.md` lists `ltx-2.3-22b-dev_embeddings_connectors.safetensors` at line 44, and `docs/ESCALATE.md` asks whether that connector requires a model patcher node at lines 20-22. The current LTX recipes never reference that connector model. Concrete fix: add a required hypothesis matrix: “missing connector node/model patcher”, “wrong CLIP type/model”, “wrong generic KSampler graph”, each with one planned test and expected result.\n\n3. [Issue 2, lines 23-31] The plan assumes the Wan recipes are video recipes whose frame count can be tuned, but the prompt graphs do not pass `frames` into any node. Example: `recipes/wan_ti2v_high.json` declares `frames: 25` at line 9, but the executable graph uses `EmptyLatentImage` with width/height/batch only at lines 60-66 and `CreateVideo` with only `images` and `fps` at lines 108-116. Concrete fix: either re-scope these as still/image smoke workflows or specify the actual video latent/conditioning node path where frame count is applied. verify: exact ComfyUI node semantics for the intended Wan video workflow.\n\n4. [Issue 2, lines 24-31] The re-test story is missing the core mechanism. `run_recipe.py` blocks only by `results/<recipe>.json` filename and `peak_vram_gb` at `run_recipe.py` lines 361-372; it has no recipe/config hash, so editing width/frames/steps still looks like an “unchanged re-run.” Concrete fix: define a config identity policy before build: add a recipe hash to receipts and have Preflight #7 block only if the current hash matches the failing measured hash, or require new recipe variant names for modified configs.\n\n5. [Issue 2, lines 25-27] The plan trusts result receipts that are internally corrupt. `results/wan_i2v_14b_low.json` is stored under the 14B filename but says `\"recipe\": \"wan_ti2v_low\"` at line 2; `results/wan_i2v_14b_high.json` says `\"recipe\": \"wan_ti2v_high\"` at line 2. Concrete fix: repair or invalidate these receipts before drawing optimization conclusions, and add receipt filename-vs-payload consistency validation to the plan.\n\nSHOULD-FIX:\n1. [Context & Invariants, lines 3-7] The boot lane says Torch includes SageAttention, but repo rules and runtime require a sage-free lane for this lab. `run_recipe.py` rejects `--use-sage-attention` at lines 415-422, and `BOOT.md` says the boot is sage-free by construction at lines 27-29. Concrete fix: state “SageAttention installed but boot lane must be sage-free” to remove the architectural contradiction.\n\n2. [Issue 2, lines 30-31] “lowering resolution, frame count, or block swapping” mixes cheap parameter sweeps with subsystem changes. Block swapping assumes node support and graph compatibility that the document does not establish. [ASSUMPTION] Concrete fix: make the first pass a bounded recipe-variant sweep using already-present nodes; defer block swapping until a specific node/API is verified in `/object_info`.\n\n3. [Issue 1, lines 9-21] The document omits acceptance criteria for an LTX fix. `RESULTS.md` classifies LTX as `ERROR`, not VRAM fail, at lines 14-16, so a successful fix must first complete execution, then run warm-cache gating. Concrete fix: add exit criteria: one cold complete render, then second consecutive warm run with peak <= 14.5 GB per `run_recipe.py` warm-pass logic at lines 710-731.\n\n4. [Issue 2, lines 23-31] The plan does not distinguish completed over-budget renders from execution errors. `results/wan_ti2v_high.json` completed with output at lines 4 and 11, but the 14B receipts show `FAIL (execution error)` and empty output at `results/wan_i2v_14b_low.json` lines 4 and 11 and `results/wan_i2v_14b_high.json` lines 4 and 11. Concrete fix: separate “VRAM optimization candidates” from “graph/runtime error candidates.”\n\nOPTIONAL / NICE-TO-HAVE:\n- Add a one-page decision table with columns: recipe, current failure class, likely root cause, first test, success gate, rollback condition.\n- Include `models_manifest.md` references for every proposed model/connector so zero-download constraints stay visible.\n\nCUT THESE (scope / over-engineering):\n1. [Issue 2, line 30] Cut “block swapping” from the first build. It is safe to cut because the current blocker is recipe/receipt validity and a sub-1 GB VRAM overage; no verified block-swap node path is specified.\n\n2. [Issue 2, line 30] Cut 14B high optimization until 14B low has a clean, correctly labeled receipt and a real completed output. Safe because `results/wan_i2v_14b_high.json` is mislabeled and records an execution error, not a completed over-budget render.\n\n3. [Issue 1, lines 19-21] Cut audio-conditioned LTX from this immediate plan unless it is explicitly part of the target deliverable. Safe because `ltx_i2v_low` and `ltx_i2v_high` already fail on the base wiring path; audio adds another connector surface before the base graph is proven."}}
